// traits
modifier.ecological.name=Ecological
modifier.ecological.desc=§oGreen Power!§r\nRenewable resources are so good, they regenerate by themselves!
modifier.cheap.name=Cheap
modifier.cheap.desc=§oMore bang for your buck!§r\nIncreases durability gained when repairing the tool.
modifier.cheapskate.name=Cheapskate
modifier.cheapskate.desc=§oCheeky!§r\nStone is bad. Your tool has less durability.
modifier.crude.name=Crude
modifier.crude.desc=§oArmor is for cowards!§r\nBonus damage against unarmored targets.
modifier.crude.extra=Vs Unarmored: +%s
modifier.prickly.name=Prickly
modifier.prickly.desc=§oOuch!§r\nNobody is safe from those thorns, they always hurt.
modifier.spiky.name=Spiky
modifier.spiky.desc=§o200% cooler with spikes!§r\nBlocking and getting hurt deals damage to the attacker.
modifier.duritos.name=Duritae
modifier.duritos.desc=§oDoesn't taste as good as it sounds.§r\nYour tool lasts longer ...most of the time.
modifier.aridiculous.name=Aridiculous
modifier.aridiculous.desc=§oTurn up the heat!§r\nThe tool works better in hotter environments.
modifier.hellish.name=Hellish
modifier.hellish.desc=§oFrom down below!§r\nDeal bonus damage to non-Nether mobs.
modifier.hellish.extra=Vs Non-Nether: +%s
modifier.alien.name=Alien
modifier.alien.desc=§oThe stats feel off...§r\n..as if they're changing! Maybe time will tell?
modifier.enderference.name=Enderference
modifier.enderference.desc=§oAnti-Teleport!§r\nPrevents Endermen from teleporting around for a short time.
modifier.fractured.name=Fractured
modifier.fractured.desc=§oHurt!§r\nYour tools damage is increased.
modifier.splintering.name=Splintering
modifier.splintering.desc=§oA souvenir for your enemies!§r\nHit them more to deal more damage.
modifier.squeaky.name=Squeaky
modifier.squeaky.desc=§oCute.§r\nYour tool is so soft and squeaky it gained silktouch, but deals no damage.
modifier.writable.name=Writable
modifier.writable.desc=§oIntellectual!§r\nMore words. More Modifiers. It's only logical!
modifier.slimey.name=Slimey
modifier.slimey.desc=§oEww, gooey!§r\nIt'll wash off.
modifier.magnetic.name=Magnetic
modifier.magnetic.desc=§oHow do they work?!§r\nHitting things attracts nearby things?!
modifier.baconlicious.name=Baconlicious
modifier.baconlicious.desc=§oBACON!§r\nHitting things sometimes gives bacon.
modifier.tasty.name=Tasty
modifier.tasty.desc=§oOm Nom Nom§r\nSmells so good.. You'd rather eat your tool than starve.
modifier.momentum.name=Momentum
modifier.momentum.desc=§oFaster, keep going!§r\nMining blocks increases your speed, as long as you keep going.
modifier.lightweight.name=Lightweight
modifier.lightweight.desc=§oSwift like the wind!§r\nIncreases the overall speed of your tool when mining and attacking.
modifier.lightweight.extra=Bonus Speed: +%s
modifier.stonebound.name=Stonebound
modifier.stonebound.desc=§oYour tool absolutely loves stone!§r\nThe tool mines faster as it wears out, but does less damage.
modifier.stonebound.extra=Stonebound Speed: +%s
modifier.petramor.name=Petramor
modifier.petramor.desc=§oSo much stone, must see it all!§r\nYour tool loves stone, it literally wants to absorb it (for durability).
modifier.insatiable.name=Insatiable
modifier.insatiable.desc=§oDevour!§r\nDuring combat you deal more and more damage but also consume more and more durability.
modifier.coldblooded.name=Cold-Blooded
modifier.coldblooded.desc=§oSavage!§r\nDeal increased damage to targets at full health.
modifier.established.name=Well-Established
modifier.established.desc=§oFree bonus XP!§r\nYou gain additional XP.
modifier.dense.name=Dense
modifier.dense.desc=§oHard...er.§r\nYour tool lasts longer when it has less durability.
modifier.stiff.name=Stiff
modifier.stiff.desc=§oUnmoving!§r\nBlocking reduces the damage taken even more.
modifier.sharp.name=Sharp
modifier.sharp.desc=§oCan even cut words!§r\nHitting an enemy leaves them bleeding for a short time.
modifier.splitting.name=Splitting
modifier.splitting.desc=§oTwo for one!§r\nThe sudden acceleration of releasing an arrow might cause it to split into two.
modifier.raging.name=Raging
modifier.raging.desc=§oA desperate solution!§r\nYour tool does more damage the lower your health is.
modifier.poisonous.name=Poisonous
modifier.poisonous.desc=§oNot exactly lead-free!§r\nPoisons enemies on hit.
modifier.heavy.name=Heavy
modifier.heavy.desc=§oDo you even lift?§r\nPrevents knockback.
modifier.holy.name=Holy
modifier.holy.desc=§oRadiant!§r\nDeal bonus damage to undead enemies.
modifier.holy.extra=Vs Undead: +%s
modifier.freezing.name=Freezing
modifier.freezing.desc=§oWinter is Coming§r\nSuccessful hits slow your target more and more.
modifier.hovering.name=Hovering
modifier.hovering.desc=§oFree like the wind§r\nProjectiles move slower but don't mind gravity as much.
modifier.breakable.name=Breakable
modifier.breakable.desc=§oThis side up!§r\nProjectiles have a 50% chance to break on impact.

// modifiers
modifier.bane_of_arthopods.name=Bane of Arthropods
modifier.bane_of_arthopods.desc=§oAnti-Spider!§r\nDeal massive damage to spiders.
modifier.bane_of_arthopods.extra=Vs Spiders: +%s
modifier.bane_of_arthopods.text=Striking a spider with its own eyeball causes it to recoil in fear. Got a pest problem? Here is the solution. Kills bugs dead.
modifier.bane_of_arthopods.effect=Deals massive damage to spiders and silverfish
modifier.beheading.name=Beheading
modifier.beheading.desc=§oOff with his head!§r\nEach level adds a 10% chance to get the enemies head on kill.
modifier.beheading.text=Working an ender pearl and some obsidian on a weapon has the curious effect of separating the target's head from its body. Just a little off the top?
modifier.beheading.effect=Enemies drop their heads
modifier.blasting.name=Blasting
modifier.blasting.desc=§oKa-Boom!§r\nYou can break non-effective blocks like normal blocks, but they might get destroyed.
modifier.blasting.extra=Blast Power: %s
modifier.blasting.text=Blow up all the blocks! Make them go away FAST!\nYou can apply multiple levels to increase speed, but you probably lose all harvested blocks
modifier.blasting.effect=Breaks blocks fast\nAOE Tools harvest uneffective blocks too\nWill likely destroy harvested blocks
modifier.diamond.name=Diamond
modifier.diamond.desc=§oShiny!§r\nIncreased durability!
modifier.diamond.text=Adding a diamond to the edge of a tool makes it more resilient and increases what the tool can mine. Also makes a fetching fashion statement.
modifier.diamond.effect=Extra durability\nMinor stat increase\nMining level increased by one, up to Obsidian\nFabulous!
modifier.emerald.name=Emerald
modifier.emerald.desc=§oFancy!§r\nIncreases durability depending on base stats!
modifier.emerald.text=Affixing an emerald to a tool's weakest point makes it especially resilient and fabulous. Villagers may also covet your tool, be wary.
modifier.emerald.effect=50% base durability increase\nMining level increased to Iron\nOutrageous!
modifier.fiery.name=Fiery
modifier.fiery.desc=§oSo hot right now!§r\nBonus fire damage, sets your enemies on fire.
modifier.fiery.extra=Fire Damage: +%s
modifier.fiery.extra2=Burn Duration: %ss
modifier.fiery.text=Adding blaze powder to a tool gives it a fiery tinge. The weapon's edges look like embers. Sadly not bright enough to be a light source.
modifier.fiery.effect=Sets enemies on fire\nDeals additional fire damage on hit
modifier.haste.name=Haste
modifier.haste.name2=Haster
modifier.haste.name3=Hastest
modifier.haste.name4=Hastester
modifier.haste.name5=Hastestest
modifier.haste.desc=§oWeeeeeee!§r\nThe redstone impulse when using your tool motivates your tool to move even faster.
modifier.haste.extra=Bonus-Speed: +%s
modifier.haste.text=Adding redstone to a tool seems to increase its speed. Redstones mining speed effect is more potent on slower tools.\nRedstone. Crazy stuff, amiright?
modifier.haste.effect=Each redstone dust increases mining speed by a small amount
modifier.knockback.name=Knockback
modifier.knockback.desc=§oHomerun!§r\nTeach things how to fly - the cool way.
modifier.knockback.text=Attaching a piston to the tool and activating it at the right time seems to throw mobs further away.
modifier.knockback.effect=Adds extra knockback\nEach piston increases the knockback distance
modifier.luck.name=Luck
modifier.luck.desc=§oShiny!§r\nYou're getting all the nice things. And a lot of them.
modifier.luck.text=Encrusting lapis on tools is a gift to the gods of luck. They will bless your tool with great fortune and loot.\nHas to be on the projectile for ranged weapons.
modifier.luck.effect=Adds fortune or looting\nTool use has a chance to increase the luck\nNot compatible with Silky
modifier.mending_moss.name=Mending Moss
modifier.mending_moss.desc=§oIt's alive!§r\nPicked up XP is stored in the tool. It will slowly use up the XP to regenerate durability.
modifier.mending_moss.extra=Stored XP: %d
modifier.mending_moss.text=Some moss has grown on the worn out edges of your tool. Enchanting it with some XP causes it to fuse with the tool, restoring it gradually.
modifier.mending_moss.effcet=Slowly repairs the tool over time
modifier.necrotic.name=Necrotic
modifier.necrotic.desc=§oI feel so Alive!!§r\nHitting enemies returns health to you depending on damage dealt.
modifier.necrotic.extra=Lifesteal: +%s
modifier.necrotic.text=Placing the bone of a Wither Skeleton on a tool gives it nefarious life-stealing powers.
modifier.necrotic.effect=Heal when dealing damage\nAdd more bones to increase the heal
modifier.reinforced.name=Reinforced
modifier.reinforced.unbreakable=Unbreakable
modifier.reinforced.desc=§oSo strong!§r\nEach level adds a %s chance to not use durability.
modifier.reinforced.extra=Reinforced: %s
modifier.reinforced.text=Adding a reinforced plate to the tool seems to help with its durability, making it stronger.
modifier.reinforced.effect=Adds a chance to not consume durability\nStacks with previous levels of Reinforced
modifier.sharpness.name=Sharp
modifier.sharpness.name2=Sharper
modifier.sharpness.name3=Sharpest
modifier.sharpness.name4=Sharpester
modifier.sharpness.name5=Sharpestest
modifier.sharpness.desc=§oOuch!§r\nSo sharp, it hurts to look at it.
modifier.sharpness.text=You can use Quartz to sharpen and hone the edge of weapons. The more Quartz is used the better you can sharpen the blade. Works with blunt items as well.
modifier.sharpness.effect=Increases attack damage\nDifferent weapons scale differently
modifier.silktouch.name=Silktouch
modifier.silktouch.desc=§oSmooth as silk!§r\nMined blocks drop themselves instead of the usual items.
modifier.silktouch.text=Adding a large glob of gold and a bunch of string seems to give the tool silky-smooth properties.\nI can't believe it's not butter!
modifier.silktouch.effect=Allows blocks to be harvested directly\nNot compatible with Luck or Autosmelt
modifier.mod_autosmelt.name=Autosmelt
modifier.mod_autosmelt.desc=§oA furnace in tool form!§r\nHarvested blocks get smelted.
modifier.mod_autosmelt.text=Melting a lava crystal onto the end of a tool gives it the power of a furnace.
modifier.mod_autosmelt.effect=Smelts blocks as they're harvested\nNot compatible with Silk Touch or the trait version of Autosmelt\nDoes not work for weapons
modifier.webbed.name=Webbed
modifier.webbed.desc=§oYuck!§r\nEntangle your foes in cobwebs, slowing them.
modifier.webbed.text=All those sticky spider webs have to be good for something. Slow your enemies with them!
modifier.webbed.effect=Each level increases slow duration\nSlow-motion
modifier.smite.name=Smite
modifier.smite.desc=§oFor Justice!§r\nDeal massive damage to undead.
modifier.smite.extra=Vs Undead: +%s
modifier.smite.text=The raw power of consecrated soil empowers your weapon, smiting enemies from on high.
modifier.smite.effect=Deals massive damage to undead enemies
modifier.fortify.name=Fortified
modifier.fortify.desc=§oHarder, better, faster, stronger!§r\nMining level increased to the same level as %s.
modifier.fortify.text=Harder, better, faster, stronger! Applies the same mining level of the material used to the tool.
modifier.fortify.effect=Increases Mining level\nMining Level depends on material used\nCan also downgrade level
modifier.fins.name=Fins
modifier.fins.desc=§oSomething's fishy...§r\nAttaching fins to the projectiles makes them travel like normal underwater.
modifier.fins.text=Let's take a fish... and strap it onto arrows. Of course! It makes them swim underwater! Now you can shoot stuff underwater!
modifier.fins.effect=Projectiles ignore water\nLogical\nMakes sense

