tinkersreborn.manuals.materialsandyou.welcome.title=The Lost Page
tinkersreborn.manuals.materialsandyou.welcome1=Welcome to the §m first §r second edition of Materials and You: Surviving the first day and beyond. Within these pages you will find the first steps to making the tools and materials you need to survive.\n\nThis book is a magic copy; it updates whenever the original has been modified. Check back occasionally for information on new things.\n\nThe first step in making tools is crafting a blank pattern. It is a blank slate to stamp a shape into, providing a reference for future creations.
tinkersreborn.manuals.materialsandyou.welcome2=You can then shape a material in a part builder with the pattern, then combine parts in the tool station. Patterns can be stored and accessed in the cast chest.
tinkersreborn.manuals.materialsandyou.partbuilder.intro=Once you have created some patterns, create the part builder to get started with tool making.
tinkersreborn.manuals.materialsandyou.partbuilder=To make a part: simply grab a blank stencil, put it in the stencil slot, select what tool part you are wanting to make, insert a soft material you can shape with your hands, and grab your part.
tinkersreborn.manuals.materialsandyou.toolstation.intro=Hopefully you still have some patterns leftover. If not can always make more.\n\nPut this here, and that there, and oh that's backwards. Better keep tinkering.
tinkersreborn.manuals.materialsandyou.toolstation=To finish the first step in your grand tinkering adventure, it is time to craft your first tool. It may not start off the best, but it is your work, and you should be proud of it.\n\nOnce you have acquired all the parts you need to make a tool, construction can begin! First get a Tinker Station, then select which tool you want to make and tinker away! Give it a name before you miss your chance.\n\nYou can also use the Tinker Station to add modifiers to your tools. The basic table only has enough room to combine three parts maximum, meaning no broad tools can be crafted. Other master tinkers know the secret to making tools out of four or five parts.
tinkersreborn.manuals.materialsandyou.storagechest.title=Storage Chests
tinkersreborn.manuals.materialsandyou.storagechest=So, you want to store your extra parts in a special chest, eh? If not, too bad you have the option anyway.\n\nPart chests allow you to store an abundance of extra parts you may have. Each slot can hold a stack of 8 parts max. If you need more than that, you're doing something wrong or have very convoluted recipes.\n\nOh, that chest is too restrictive? Try the tinkers' chest! It can store any item in a total of 64 slots, though each slot holds just 16 items.
tinkersreborn.manuals.materialsandyou.partchest=Never know when you might need that unused tool part again later.
tinkersreborn.manuals.materialsandyou.repair.title=Repairing
tinkersreborn.manuals.materialsandyou.repair=To repair tools, simply place the tool in the Tool Station or Tool Forge with the material of the head. Alternatively, you can use repair kits, which work both in crafting tables and when right clicking the tool directly!
tinkersreborn.manuals.materialsandyou.part_swap.title=Part Swapping
tinkersreborn.manuals.materialsandyou.part_swap=Ever wish you could undo a past mistake? Luckily you can on tools. If you want to change the material of one of the parts, place the tool with the desired new part in the tinker station. For tools that have multiple of the same part, try a few different slots to replace the right one. For armor, you can often swap parts using a casting table.
